Z||000000||loren||01-13-2001||09:03 PM||||Is changing the pin in a door hinge very difficult?<BR>I am 70 yrs old and just purchased my first Fiero,an 85 GT. now all i need is to get my wife on board so that i don't get divorced or shot at.<BR>This is an awsome forum...i am impressed.<BR>Loren<BR> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-13-2001||10:35 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>When you redo the hinge pins make sure you put in new bushings.  New pins are worthless without new bushings.  Overall, it wasnt that difficult for me and my dad, but we have done a few other doors.  The most trouble we had was getting the spring back into it's place.  Try to get a helper.  If you have trouble finding the door hardware, rodney dickman sells it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
